  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.5856 acc, while image-only (config_025) gets only 0.2596, confirming RNA is the dominant signal. The current best uses PCA (a linear, unlearned encoder) for RNA. Question: Would a learned RNA encoder (scgpt) improve representation quality and thus validation accuracy, holding all other components (imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, multiprofile) constant? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001. Rationale: Since RNA drives most of the signal, upgrading its encoder is the highest-impact single change to test. With 7 experiments remaining, isolating the RNA encoder effect now will inform whether subsequent experiments should focus on learned vs. linear RNA representations or pivot to other components."
